---

transposer drives several third-party projects, which it fetches rather than
vendors. They keep their own licences:

  Audiveris   AGPL-3.0   https://github.com/Audiveris/audiveris
  Mozart      Apache-2.0 https://github.com/aashrafh/Mozart
  oemer       MIT        https://github.com/BreezeWhite/oemer
  music21     BSD-3      https://github.com/cuthbertLab/music21
  Verovio     LGPL-2.1   https://github.com/rism-digital/verovio

Audiveris is AGPL-3.0. Running it as a separate program, which is what this
project does, does not place transposer under the AGPL -- but if you build a
network service on top of it, read the AGPL's terms for yourself.
